PKG=a409130
NAME=a4091-k30 1.0.0-11 - A4091/A4092/A4770 SCSI driver module (root class), k30 line
ARCH=Amiga
VERSION=1.0.0-11
CATEGORY=system
CLASSES=none
VENDOR=amix
PSTAMP=amix-a409130-1.0.0-11
# Kernel space (amix-dlm C2-2, C3-5 v10 sec 1, C4-2): a role=module entry of
# the #ext kpkg block (line=k30, kabi=k30.1.2), class root, never an ordinary
# entry.  Catalog name a4091-k30, pkginst a409130; VERSION is the module's
# own release (kernel/drivers/a4091/module/VERSION), the same on both lines.
# 1.0.0-11 carries module 1.0.0-8 (completion on the 53C710's interrupt
# after a self-test; param intr), built with gcc-cross-amix 33ebadc (cc=gcc-2.7.2.3-33ebadc).
APKG_DESC=A4091/A4092/A4770 SCSI (NCR 53C710) as a root-class kernel module for the 68030 root-class module kernel kernel-k30-m (kabi k30.1.2): /etc/conf/mod.d/a4091. DMA through the core's 030 provider. Needs kernel-k30-m -68 or later (cc=gcc-2.7.2.3-33ebadc).
DESC=The kernel/drivers/a4091 driver built as an amix-dlm kernel module for the 68030 line (kabi k30.1.2): root class, loaded by the module core's root pass before the root filesystem is mounted when an A4091, A4092 or A4770 is present (match zorro:0202:54, zorro:c0de:01, zorro:c0de:02), up to four boards registered with sd at rank zorro; commands complete on the chip's interrupt (level 2) once a self-test after the root mount passes, else polled (param intr=0: always polled); never unloaded; DMA through the core's DDI 1.2 (C4-5 v5), on k30 the core's 030 provider (a bounce pool below 0x08000000): needs kernel-k30-m -68 or later, whose pin is the module's cc=gcc-2.7.2.3-33ebadc, and the boot loader of amix 1.1 or later; a transfer the provider cannot reach is refused, not armed.  No major and no device nodes of its own: sd owns the disk majors and nodes.  /etc/conf/modreg.d/a4091 holds the package's defaults (none: intr keeps the module's 1).  The package writes no boot store; after the install apkg runs kbootset build and commit (or prints the command when bootset=manual).  MIT.
